// =============================================================================
// history-course — "Historical Truth: American History in the Light of the Word"
// =============================================================================
// Darrell, 2026-09-22: "We need history to reflect actual history!!!!! Courses
// on Historical Truth Light from Yahweh's perspectives explicitly and
// comprehensive summary... American Historical accuracy from the beginning...
// least of these and fatherless and widows narratives... two or more gather
// together there He will be in the midst..." And: "Lessons about History need
// to be organized and we need to fill whatever gaps we have." Measured before
// this was built: the school had ten departments and no History department; no
// course in the catalog taught American history at all. This is the first
// course of the department.
//
// THE ARC, and it is one argument in eight moves — the same shape the Real
// Estate department opened with, because the reason is the same: a subject
// this charged must be taught under His frame before any other frame:
//   1. The standard before the story (Psalms 119:160; Deuteronomy 32:7; Psalms 78)
//   2. The fatherless, the widow and the stranger — His measure of a nation
//      (Deuteronomy 10:18-19; Exodus 22:21-24; Matthew 25:40)
//   3. The landmark and the vineyard — how land is taken by lawful steps
//      (Deuteronomy 19:14; 1 Kings 21; Micah 2:1-2)
//   4. The wage that could not wait — bondage, and the law that forbade it
//      (Leviticus 19:13; Deuteronomy 24:14-15; Exodus 21:16; Deuteronomy 23:15-16)
//   5. Two weights in one bag — one law written two ways
//      (Deuteronomy 25:13-16; Isaiah 10:1-2; Leviticus 19:15)
//   6. The fields of the fatherless — the narratives of the least of these
//      (Proverbs 23:10-11; Deuteronomy 24:19-21; Ruth 2:2; Malachi 3:5)
//   7. No respecter of persons — the standard the founders wrote and did not keep
//      (Acts 10:34-35; Acts 17:26; Genesis 1:27; Deuteronomy 1:17)
//   8. Two or three witnesses — how true history is established, and Who is
//      in the midst of the gathering (Deuteronomy 19:15; Matthew 18:16, 20)
//
// The standard → the measure → the land → the labour → the law → the least →
// the person → the witnesses. Lesson 8 is where his own word lands: "where two
// or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them"
// (Matthew 18:20) — the family and the church telling what happened, with
// their witnesses, is how a true history is kept, and He is in that room.
//
// TEACH THE WORD, DO NOT DEBATE IT (DR-0098) — and SPEAK ESTABLISHED FACT
// (DR-0100). Every American fact in this course is documented history stated
// plainly with its date: the 1619 landing, the Indian Removal Act of 1830, the
// three-fifths clause, the 1860 census count, the Fugitive Slave Act of 1850,
// the Thirteenth Amendment and its exception clause, Plessy in 1896, the HOLC
// maps of the 1930s, Greenwood in 1921, Brown in 1954, the Acts of 1964, 1965
// and 1968. Where a count is genuinely unsettled (the Tulsa dead) the course
// says so narrowly; it never smears "contested" over what is documented, and
// it never stages two schools of opinion for the reader to pick from. The Word
// is the authority; the record is read under it.
//
// AGE BANDS FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0497 / DR-0498). Every lesson carries
// levels.teen and levels.senior, authored, measured on the ladder, the
// fullness floor and the overlap ceiling.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). Every quoted span was
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own public-domain KJV
// (app/public/bible/kjv/*.json) and is re-pinned by history-course.test.js, so
// a later edit cannot drift the text and still ship. Our own prose says
// Yahweh; the quotations are left exactly as the KJV has them, "the LORD"
// included (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR THE RECORD — carried on the meta so every
// surface renders the limit with the course. This course teaches how to read
// history under the Word and gives the documented facts it names; it is not a
// complete history of the United States, and every date in it can be checked
// against the primary record it points to.
// =============================================================================

